# "Up to one target Equipment": Raubahn's attack trigger needs only its attacking creature. On turn 3 Bot1 has an Equipment it
# could attach, the Bloodforged Battle-Axe on the Ornithopter that stays home, and chooses none (`Bot1.Target()`) with Raubahn
# as the attacking creature: the trigger still goes on the stack and resolves, and the Axe stays where it was, Raubahn
# remains a 2/2 and Bot2 takes 2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mountain
Raubahn, Bull of Ala Mhigo
Bloodforged Battle-Axe
Ornithopter
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Raubahn, Bull of Ala Mhigo.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bloodforged Battle-Axe.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Bloodforged Battle-Axe.Activate(Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Raubahn, Bull of Ala Mhigo > Bot2)
Bot1.Target()
Bot1.Target(Raubahn, Bull of Ala Mhigo)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Bloodforged Battle-Axe.AttachedTo = Ornithopter
? Bot1.Battlefield.Raubahn, Bull of Ala Mhigo.Power = 2
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Life = 18

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Bloodforged Battle-Axe.AttachedTo = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 2
Bot2.Life = 18
